From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:46:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the threaded WAL Home alive through teardown

A pending home task can hold an actor whose shipper and SQLite close callback borrow the WAL channel. Cancel home tasks before releasing actors and the isolate copy, then release the channel. Own the thread spare descriptor until task cleanup ends.

Exercise scope teardown with a real actor and SQLite connection, an unresolved task and lifetime markers that can report an early release safely.

